=== reading ===
  Two-layer structure: the touch is thin and asymmetric (median
  imbalance 0.79; a <=10-contract retail order IS the best quote
  on one side in 20% of snapshots) while ~20K contracts per side
  stand within 5c — 11x the touch, twice as balanced — on ~90
  games at once, ~2M contracts standing. Two-sided size
  at that scale is professional market-making, not organic peer
  supply. Public data has no member IDs, so Kalshi Trading's own
  share cannot be measured; the documentary record (rulebook,
  CFTC 2026-07-30 proposal) establishes the affiliate is among
  these quoters, restricted to bona fide two-sided making. The
  economics: takers surrender ~5% to settlement and the quoting
  layer collects it — dealer-like revenue inside a peer-to-peer
  shell, without directional exposure if the bona fide rules bind.
